#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:10
msgid "Scope"
msgstr "Hatókör"

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:12
msgid ""
"This chunk covers 13 entrypoint modules (4,607 lines; 42,045 measured "
"o200k_base proxy tokens). I read every assigned line. The source spans "
"production operation registration, spreadsheet verification, overview "
"evidence/read ports, migration notices, profile archive and quickfile "
"composition, review-package custody, runtime management, workbench "
"generation, workflow-run reads, and workstation checks. Static inspection"
" only: I did not import or execute application modules or run tests. This"
" chunk contains no test files, so runtime behavior and end-to-end caller "
"invariants remain unverified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:14
msgid "Product capabilities"
msgstr "Termékképességek"

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:16
msgid ""
"The central composition module builds the production operation registry "
"by assembling definitions for profile, ledger, invoice, evidence, tax-"
"model, overview, runtime-adjacent and other workflows, then creates "
"matching public registrations and sorts both by stable definition IDs. It"
" exposes this registry to the operation service graph, which receives one"
" pinned authority operation, a journal, lease repository, secure operand "
"custody, random owner and lease tokens, and bounded execution/cleanup "
"settings. The declared design is one immutable graph with authority "
"supplied by the caller; construction itself does not open a browser or "
"start a supervised operation (registry "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/operation_composition.py`), service composition"
" (`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/operation_composition.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:18
msgid ""
"Specialized compositions give operators a path through Google Sheets "
"exports, profile archives, quickfile work, review-package exchange, "
"overviews, workbench generation, and local workstation checks. "
"Spreadsheet operations bind a profile-scoped calculation snapshot, "
"prepare provider access only after checking local Drive configuration, "
"then calculate or verify against the same snapshot. Apply-capable "
"verification calls its pre-mutation boundary before remote writes and "
"reports the written-cell result; a report must match the snapshot model, "
"period, and revision (spreadsheet ports "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/modelo_spreadsheet_operation_composition.py`))."
" Profile archive supports local capsule export, reconciliation of "
"prepared exports through an injected writer, and optional mirror push. "
"Push checks the exact profile, resolves the Google export capability and "
"Drive root, and wraps provider creation in an admitted handoff; it also "
"supports dry-run and namespace/row limits (archive ports "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/profile_archive_operation_composition.py`)). "
"Quickfile assembles calculation, verification, export, diagnostics/read, "
"certificate, operator-probe, and attachment capabilities for one profile "
"and routes secure-object mutations through the supplied writer (quickfile"
" ports (`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/quickfile_operation_composition.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:20
msgid ""
"Review-package exchange binds signing, encryption, recipient fingerprint,"
" replay-guard, event-history, and explicit local-file adapters to one "
"profile. Final local writes are fenced by the operation writer; reads "
"load operator-authorized inputs into transient memory. Secure-object "
"revision conflicts are translated at the writer boundary and restored to "
"the adapter’s canonical conflict type so its established winner-"
"read/retry logic can run (exchange ports "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/review_package_exchange_operation_composition.py`),"
" profile binding "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/review_package_exchange_operation_composition.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:22
msgid ""
"The overview read port captures status, calendar, agenda, backlog, "
"explanation, or preparation data from one active profile under the "
"caller’s pinned registry operation. Calendar and status combine schedule-"
"derived obligations with local event, filing, work-unit, and history "
"evidence. Optional evidence-load failures generally return warning "
"notices and continue with a schedule-only view, whose documented "
"degradation direction is to leave obligations visible rather than "
"silently suppress them (canonical read capture "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/overview_read_composition.py`), calendar "
"composition (`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/overview_read_composition.py`), "
"evidence degradation "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/overview_evidence_composition.py`)). Filing "
"evidence is more selective: stored registry coordinates must still be "
"confirmable through the pinned authority, and a stored justificante "
"artefact must match recorded byte length and digest, parse successfully, "
"and agree on model, year, period, and expected identity before its CSV is"
" used (artefact verification "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/overview_evidence_composition.py`), matching "
"checks (`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/overview_evidence_composition.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:24
msgid ""
"Workbench generation combines profile, ledger, calculation, filing, "
"notification-custody, declaration-result, calendar, and operation-"
"contract readers. It resolves each work unit at calculation grade first "
"and falls back to static inspection only when the graded read returns a "
"taxpayer-facing refusal; it retries a changing workspace at most three "
"times and raises a typed contention error if no stable read is obtained "
"(provider composition "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/workbench_generation_composition.py`), "
"graded/static projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/workbench_generation_composition.py`)). Runtime"
" management offers passive listener/manager inspection, explicit start "
"and login-autostart configuration, and a two-step stop-consent object. "
"Stop confirmation stays on the preview’s verified connection, is single-"
"use, checks request, boot, and connection IDs, and exposes uncertainty "
"separately from a validated acceptance; acceptance itself is not treated "
"as proof that shutdown has drained (inspection "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/runtime_management.py`), stop consent "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/runtime_management.py`), preview "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/runtime_management.py`)). The workstation-check"
" composition performs local probes and does not request a provider "
"handoff (workstation check "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/workstation_check_operation_composition.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:26
msgid "Knowledge and data"
msgstr "Tudás és adatok"

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:28
msgid ""
"These modules mostly orchestrate information owned by domain and "
"application layers rather than embedding tax rules. Overview obligations "
"are built by schedule and applicability services; local event, filed-"
"declaration, calculation, work-unit, and justificante records enrich the "
"read. Filed-declaration evidence is linked to registry revision "
"coordinates and validated artefact hashes, but this code does not "
"establish the current legal correctness of the underlying schedule or "
"registry. Spreadsheet and workbench projections likewise inherit "
"calculation authority from a pinned operation. A workflow-run read port "
"binds its repository to a normalized UUID profile bucket, and pipeline "
"reads verify that the requested profile matches the active bucket before "
"loading profile-grounded calculation and verification repositories "
"(pipeline reader "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/overview_pipeline_composition.py`), workflow-"
"run reader (`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/workflow_run_composition.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:30
msgid ""
"The payer-fact notice module prevents a profile migration from making a "
"cleared “false” look like a newly arising obligation. It maps cleared "
"profile paths to setup-flow question IDs, emits yes/no CLI flags, and can"
" re-emit notices only while the active record has unanswered cleared "
"paths. An optional modelo filter limits notices to rules gated by that "
"fact (notice construction "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/payer_fact_migration_notices.py`), pending "
"paths (`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/payer_fact_migration_notices.py`)). These"
" notices are user guidance derived from local schema and applicability "
"metadata, not legal confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:32
msgid "Security and safety assessment"
msgstr "Biztonsági és biztonságossági értékelés"

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:34
msgid ""
"The chunk repeatedly binds repositories to an explicit UUID bucket and "
"retained authority, checks the active profile at operation boundaries, "
"and uses injected mutation writers for guarded commits. Archive push "
"gates external storage capability before credentials/provider "
"construction; spreadsheet writes have a pre-mutation hook; review-package"
" final outputs pass through an operation writer. Runtime stop consent "
"retains and reuses the exact connection on which the preview was issued, "
"rejects replay, settles in-flight confirmation before release, and "
"preserves cleanup errors across cancellation. These are concrete "
"protections at these composition boundaries, while provider, repository, "
"worker, and OS guarantees live in modules outside this chunk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:36
msgid ""
"A local calendar-survey defect is directly visible: "
"_calendar_other_profiles reuses the name bucket_id for each pointer in "
"its comprehension and tests bucket_id != bucket_id. That predicate is "
"always false, so the survey’s locked-profile collection is always empty, "
"regardless of other profiles present (survey filter "
"(`src/cadrumo/entrypoints/overview_read_composition.py`)). This finding "
"is limited to the locked-profile projection; it does not establish that "
"other profile data is read or that single-profile calendar contents are "
"wrong. Correct the shadowed variable and add a focused test with at least"
" one other profile pointer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:38
msgid "Implementation assessment and follow-up"
msgstr "Az implementáció értékelése és további vizsgálatok"

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:40
msgid ""
"The strongest quality pattern is the separation between composition and "
"business policy: one registry graph wires typed operations, while focused"
" modules bind profile repositories, authority pins, provider access, and "
"writer callbacks. Overview evidence is treated as enrichment and failures"
" are surfaced through notices; sensitive filing artefacts are verified "
"before their parsed result is admitted. The runtime stop flow "
"distinguishes accepted, refused, uncertain, and released states instead "
"of equating an acknowledgement with settled shutdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:42
msgid ""
"The central operation composition is very large and imports and registers"
" a broad set of operation families in one module. Its explicit sorted "
"registry helps keep a stable public surface, but the breadth makes "
"omissions and wiring drift harder to review; synthesis should compare "
"definitions with registrations and confirm every public registration "
"reaches the intended exact-profile worker. Cross-module review should "
"also establish that the calendar profile survey’s filtered pointer "
"behavior is tested, all writer callbacks cover the actual irreversible "
"writes, and cancellation cleanup behavior remains sound across the "
"runtime transport adapters. No tests were run and no end-to-end behavior "
"is certified by this static pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:44
msgid "Dependencies and follow-up"
msgstr "Függőségek és további vizsgálatok"

#: ../../technical/articles/155-entrypoint-operation-and-read-composition.md:46
msgid ""
"The principal dependencies are the operation registry/service layer, "
"secure-object and profile repositories, pinned calculation authority, "
"overview schedule/evidence builders, AEAT artefact parsers, Google "
"storage admission, review-package custody adapters, workbench workspace "
"resolvers, and native runtime endpoint/manager implementations. Synthesis"
" should resolve registry registration coverage and worker profile "
"lifetime with those modules, and verify the calendar-survey defect with a"
" focused regression test. Legal freshness, actual provider/OS behavior, "
"and production database guarantees are outside the evidence in this "
"chunk."
msgstr ""

